re are enough samples for refit... PyDESeq2 docs say: \"If refit_cooks=True, genes with Cook's outliers are refit with a design without the outlier sample; requires at least 2 samples per condition?\" Let's not worry; the task explicitly says refit_cooks=True.\n\nNow let's write the script. Should we also compute a quick sanity check with an independent lightweight method? The instructions say \"one main method + one lightweight independent verification\". Verification = a schema assertion script, plus possibly a sanity check: number of genes tested == number after prefilter (minus internal drops), padj null count, recompute passing genes from CSV to verify consistency. Implement the verification as a separate lightweight check (part of the final schema assertion step). Re-read the output CSV and independently verify the prefilter count from raw counts (recompute the keep mask), confirming they match.\n\nNow let's write analysis.py.\n\nAlso, for robustness of JSON serialization: convert numpy types with a custom default.\n\nEdge case: pvalue could be NaN for some genes (e.g., due to extreme Cook's outliers or zero dispersion). Keep as empty/null.\n\nSignificance determination:\n```\nsig = res[\"padj\"].notna() & (res[\"padj\"] < 0.05) & (res[\"log2FoldChange\"].abs() > 0.5) & (res[\"baseMean\"] > 10)\n```\n\nWrite CSV with `res.to_csv(..., index_label=\"gene_id\")`. Column order: gene_id, gene_name, baseMean, log2FoldChange, lfcSE, stat, pvalue, padj.\n\nNow, let's write the file."}}
